   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- Performances featured Stroker Ace, Buckingham Green, Mutilated Lips, and Roses are Free [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **ween00-06-22d1t01**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **ween00-06-22d1t02**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **ween00-06-22d1t03**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **ween00-06-22d1t04**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **ween00-06-22d1t05**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **ween00-06-22d1t06**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **ween00-06-22d1t07**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **ween00-06-22d1t08**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **ween2000-06-22.akg391.shnf** (recommended): source not stated; 42 songs; 192 min [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **ween2000-06-22.akg391.shnf**: taped by Tyler Bradford; transferred by Brian Walker; source: AKG 391s (NOS) > AKG B18 P/S > Sony M-1 [1]. Also: Recorded with AKG 391s into Sony M-1, transferred via Montego II+ to CDrWIN [1]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Fan art by www.inmusicwetrust.com: [In Music We Trust - SHOW REVIEW: Ween: Vancouver BC - June 22, 2000](https://www.inmusicwetrust.com/articles/33h08.html) [3]",
